# drivers/display/conf (b651): the e-ink panel's controller.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver EPD
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.epd.c
	help    /dev/hakios-epd, the panel's EPD controller as a character device (epd=1): four commands, a marker and
	help    its waiter. A skeleton: the controller's address, register layout and waveform blob are not known yet, so
	help    nothing is driven until they are (devices/b651/EPDC.md)

driver FB
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.fb.c
	help    /dev/hakios-fb, the panel writable from user space (fbdev=1): the framebuffer the text console and
	help    virtio_gpu=1 already share, with a geometry ioctl, a blit, and write() as a pixel stream. This is what
	help    makes a picture drawn by a program visible at all; it rasterises nothing (devices/b651/SIM.md)
